{"id":"ai-terminal-ysr","content_hash":"6977dd54560b7821a355ac606c77e7861252832887a8e02ba21a1b38e0022a63","title":"Decouple fencing/truncation from REPL","description":"Context: Agent B currently emits raw stdout in final messages (e.g., cycle 5aaef586), and the REPL adds fences/truncation based on output_value_types. This means the REPL is adding content instead of just presenting. Problem: REPL should be a dumb presenter; fencing/truncation and block decisions should come from orchestrator/agents. We need to design an upstream contract where Agent B/orchestrator provide explicit segments/placeholders with tags and any truncation instructions, leaving REPL to render faithfully. Status: Solution open; needs upstream contract/prompt redesign and UI changes aligned with spec v1.5.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-20T15:41:54.811125881-05:00","updated_at":"2025-11-22T16:24:11.190028287Z","closed_at":"2025-11-22T16:24:11.190028287Z","source_repo":"."}
